# Opus R14-B: keep the bytes the documents hash. git's global core.autocrlf=true on grok-pc would check text out with
# CRLF, so a fresh clone would show other sha256 values than RESULTS.md / HANDOFF.md name: code, scripts, docs and
# committed inputs stay LF in every checkout; logs, patches and raw outputs stay byte-exact as committed.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=lf
*.cpp       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.tsv       text eol=lf
*.sha256    text eol=lf
**/logs/**  -text
*.patch     -text
*.jsonl     -text
